   "text": "At a twelve hour day, sunrise to sunset takes six hours. The ground under your feet now moves at about thirty-three hundred kilometers an hour, nearly three times the speed of sound. You weigh one point four percent less than on a still Earth, four times what you feel today. A seventy kilogram person feels like about sixty-nine."
